[agent] ## What was built (all in the per-run dataset `mlpab_mlpab781a9d`, region `***REDACTED***`)
[agent] **Raw feature tables (offline, BigQuery-backed feature groups)**
[agent] - `rawa55c41b` v1 — key `row_id`, feature `a_val`, loaded from `raw_a.csv` (250 rows)
[agent] - `rawb55c41b` v1 — key `row_id`, feature `b_val`, loaded from `raw_b.csv` (240 rows)
[agent] **Derived feature table**
[agent] - `derived55c41b` v1 — key `row_id`, feature `col_sum`. Built by a single BigQuery job that **INNER JOINs** the two raw tables on `row_id` and computes `ROUND(a_val + b_val, 6)`. Contains exactly the **186 row_ids present in both** sources; registered columns are exactly `row_id` (key) + `col_sum`.
[agent] **Online / low-latency access**
[agent] - The Vertex **FeatureOnlineStore** quota (project-wide max 8) was exhausted by parallel runs, so I used the platform's other online path: a Vertex **Featurestore** online-serving instance `mlpab781a9d_derived55c41b_fs` (1 serving node), entity type `derived55c41b`, feature `col_sum`, imported from the derived BQ table. Online reads confirmed (e.g. `R00005 → 5.134`). This is the platform's real-time store, distinct from the offline BigQuery-backed feature groups.
[agent] **Lineage / provenance**
[agent] - BigQuery/Dataplex captures the derivation natively from the join job, and I explicitly registered it in **Vertex ML Metadata**: execution `mlpab781a9d_derive_derived55c41b` with `rawa55c41b`, `rawb55c41b` as **INPUT** artifacts and `derived55c41b` as **OUTPUT**.
